  <prompt>Land three regression-prevention deliverables from task 202's Class-B punch list:
- **B01**: New ArchTest `Spaarke.ArchTests.ADR032.AsymmetricRegistrationTests.UnconditionalConsumerMustHaveUnconditionalDependency` — scans all `*Module.cs` DI files in `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/**/*Module.cs` for pattern: service registered inside `if (flag)` block AND some other unconditionally-registered service's ctor injects it → FAIL with specific asymmetric pair. Prevents recurrence of the SESSION 5 `e3a15db91` IActionSeam bug.
- **B02**: New nightly ArchTest scanning `AddOptions<T>.ValidateOnStart()` in BFF DI and diffing against `per_env_settings` manifest (per task 201 deferred + task 081.5 rollback). Prevents Tier-1 IOptions inventory drift where a `.ValidateOnStart()` call exists but manifest lacks the corresponding config catalog entry.
- **B15**: Add "Tier-1-IOptions deploy checklist" section to `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Systematic checklist reviewers walk when a PR adds `AddOptions<T>.ValidateOnStart()`. Also authors optional CI script that runs B02's ArchTest on PR (main-session-only per Sub-Agent Write Boundary).

All three are REGRESSION-PREVENTION — no production code fix, but critical for preventing recurrence of surfaced bugs.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in: ArchUnit / ArchTest patterns (existing `Spaarke.ArchTests.*` reference); ADR-032 F.1 asymmetric-registration anti-pattern (root CLAUDE.md §10 + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` § F.1); Tier-1 IOptions `AddOptions<T>.ValidateOnStart()` fail-fast pattern (r3 task 061); SESSION 5 `e3a15db91` IActionSeam case study; `per_env_settings` manifest structure (Bicep-generated per-environment config catalog); `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` structure (`§ F.1 Asymmetric-Registration Tier 1.5 Anti-Pattern` reference format).</role>

  <goal>Three deliverables landed:
- **B01**: `tests/unit/Spaarke.ArchTests/ADR032/AsymmetricRegistrationTests.cs` exists with `UnconditionalConsumerMustHaveUnconditionalDependency` test method. Test scans all `*Module.cs` files in `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/**` for the asymmetric pattern. Test PASSES on current codebase (validates existing state clean post-`e3a15db91` fix). Test FAILS if a regression is introduced (asymmetric pair added). Test message names the specific pair (`<UnconditionalService>` ctor-injects `<ConditionalService>` registered inside `<flag>` gate).
- **B02**: `tests/nightly/Spaarke.ArchTests/IOptionsDriftTests.cs` exists with `IOptionsInventoryMustMatchManifest` test method. Test enumerates all `AddOptions<T>.ValidateOnStart()` calls in BFF DI, reads `per_env_settings` manifest (or `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` § F.2 catalog), and asserts each `T` has a corresponding manifest entry. Test PASSES on current codebase (unless drift already present — then documents drift as issue).
- **B15**: `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` has new subsection "§ F.4 Tier-1-IOptions Deploy Checklist" enumerating reviewer steps when a PR adds `AddOptions<T>.ValidateOnStart()`: (a) confirm manifest entry; (b) confirm KV binding provisioned; (c) confirm test coverage for missing-config fail-fast path; (d) run B02 ArchTest locally. Optional CI script at `scripts/ci/check-ioptions-drift.ps1` runs B02 on PR.

`dotnet test` green (new tests pass on current state); B01+B02 wired into CI (nightly for B02).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 202 SESSION 5 case study analyzed commit `e3a15db91` (IActionSeam ADR-032 F.1 asymmetric-registration bug). Root cause: `IActionSeam` registered inside compound `if (DocIntel && Analysis)` gate at `AnalysisServicesModule.cs:1425`; `CommunicationRiActionService` requires it UNCONDITIONALLY at `CommunicationModule.cs:195`. Fix landed atomically on `work/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1` (hoisted registration to top-of-module unconditional block ~line 160). SESSION 5 identified missing ArchTest: existing ADR-032 forcing-function catches "kill-switch declared" pattern but NOT "unconditional consumer + conditionally-registered dependency" pattern.

Task 201 (`h4b-bulk-appsettings-handler`) deferred an IOptions inventory-drift ArchTest during Wave G-6 authoring; task 081.5 rollback also documented `.ValidateOnStart()` chains lacking systemic CI/config-catalog cross-check.

**Why "regression prevention" not "code fix"**: the bugs are FIXED (e3a15db91 for B01; various Wave G-6/G-7 wire-ups for B02). ArchTests prevent RECURRENCE — the next time an author adds an asymmetric registration or adds `.ValidateOnStart()` without manifest entry, CI catches it at PR time instead of during E2E acceptance.

**§ F.4 name**: existing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` § F has F.1 (Asymmetric-Registration Tier 1.5 Anti-Pattern), F.2 (Fixture-Config-FIRST Inspection Protocol), F.3 (Empirical-Reproduction-FIRST Protocol). B15 adds F.4 (Tier-1-IOptions Deploy Checklist) — natural next-slot.</background>
