  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load + main-session confirm">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL, sonnet/xhigh, TEST-MODIFYING). Confirm current invocation is MAIN SESSION (not sub-agent) — B15 step will fail otherwise. Read `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B01/B02/B15 rows + case study. Read `.claude/adr/ADR-032` + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` § F.1/F.2/F.3.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Verify no existing tests/subsection">Grep `tests/` for `AsymmetricRegistrationTests` + `IOptionsDriftTests` + `IOptionsInventory` — should return zero. Grep `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` for `F.4` + `Tier-1-IOptions Deploy Checklist` — should return zero. If ANY exist → mark row `already-applied` + skip that sub-row.</step>
    <step order="2" name="B01 ArchTest author">Author `tests/unit/Spaarke.ArchTests/ADR032/AsymmetricRegistrationTests.cs`:
- Test method `UnconditionalConsumerMustHaveUnconditionalDependency`
- Enumerate all `*Module.cs` files in `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/**`
- For each, parse `services.AddSingleton<TInterface, TImpl>()` calls (or similar) grouped by lexical containment inside `if (flag) { ... }` blocks
- Build UNCONDITIONAL registration set + CONDITIONAL registration set (with flag name)
- For each UNCONDITIONAL service, use Roslyn or reflection to find its constructor dependencies
- FAIL if any UNCONDITIONAL service's ctor injects a CONDITIONAL service
- Message names the pair: `<UnconditionalService>` ctor-injects `<ConditionalService>` registered inside `<flag>` gate; hoist `<ConditionalService>` to unconditional OR apply ADR-032 F.1 Null-Object kill-switch pattern
- Include fixture demonstrating the `e3a15db91` original bug (IActionSeam inside DocIntel/Analysis compound gate) as test data — assert test would have FAILED on pre-fix code
- Header comment cites case study + KEEP path per ADR-038 §7</step>
    <step order="3" name="B01 verify passes on current codebase">`dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~AsymmetricRegistrationTests` — should PASS (post-`e3a15db91` fix state is clean). If FAILS → surfaces NEW asymmetric-registration bug not caught previously; escalate + file separate task.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Checkpoint">Run context-handoff — B01 complete, B02 + B15 remaining.</step>
    <step order="5" name="B02 nightly ArchTest author">Author `tests/nightly/Spaarke.ArchTests/IOptionsDriftTests.cs`:
- Test method `IOptionsInventoryMustMatchManifest`
- Enumerate all `AddOptions<T>.ValidateOnStart()` calls in BFF Program.cs + Infrastructure/DI/
- Read `per_env_settings` manifest (Bicep-generated OR docs/architecture/ config catalog — determine source in Step 1)
- For each `T`: assert manifest has corresponding entry (config key + KV binding declaration)
- FAIL naming missing manifest entries
- Include ArchTest opt-in pattern (nightly tag) — not in PR-blocking suite by default; wired into nightly workflow
- Header comment cites task 201 deferred + task 081.5 rollback</step>
    <step order="6" name="B02 verify + wire nightly">`dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~IOptionsDriftTests` — PASS (or report existing drift as separate issue). Add nightly wire-up in `.github/workflows/*.yml` under nightly-tests job (or create new nightly workflow if none).</step>
    <step order="7" name="B15 § F.4 authoring (MAIN SESSION ONLY)">Add new subsection to `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` after § F.3:

```
### F.4 Tier-1-IOptions Deploy Checklist (binding, added 2026-08-24 by task 204e per punch list B15 + task 081.5 rollback)

When a PR adds `AddOptions<T>.ValidateOnStart()` in BFF DI, the reviewer applies:

1. **Manifest entry**: confirm `per_env_settings` manifest has corresponding config key + KV binding declaration for T's required fields.
2. **KV binding provisioned**: confirm Bicep provisions KV secret + App Service reference (`@Microsoft.KeyVault(...)`) for any secret fields in T.
3. **Fail-fast test coverage**: unit test asserts BFF `/health` returns unhealthy at startup when a required field is missing.
4. **Local ArchTest run**: reviewer runs `dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~IOptionsDriftTests` locally before approving; nightly CI (B02) catches drift going forward.

Failure to apply this checklist has resulted in production standup false-starts (r3 task 081.5 rollback + SESSION 5 Model 1 Prod BFF gates).

Reference: task 202 punch list B15; ArchTest B02 at `tests/nightly/Spaarke.ArchTests/IOptionsDriftTests.cs`.
```

Author optional CI wrapper `scripts/ci/check-ioptions-drift.ps1` that invokes B02 (PR-time opt-in via label).</step>
    <step order="8" name="Build + verify all three">`dotnet build tests/` — 0 warnings 0 errors. `dotnet test --filter Category=Unit` — B01 green. `dotnet test --filter Category=Nightly` — B02 green (or documents pre-existing drift).</step>
    <step order="8.5" name="Quality gates">FULL rigor + TEST-MODIFYING → invoke `code-review` + `adr-check` skills per root CLAUDE.md §8. Address any Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Report">Update `current-task.md` + `TASK-INDEX.md`; annotate `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B01/B02/B15 rows: `applied 2026-XX-XX task 204e — <ArchTest path | § F.4 subsection>`.</step>
  </steps>

